---
/**
 * Standing disclaimer. docs/04-compliance.md requires this class of notice on
 * every results surface and every page that discusses backup power.
 * It is not decoration: the wording is a liability boundary.
 */
interface Props {
  /** Adds the medical-adjacency paragraph for CPAP and other therapy pages. */
  medical?: boolean;
  /** Adds the backfeed / panel warning for home-backup content. */
  electrical?: boolean;
}

const { medical = false, electrical = false } = Astro.props;
---

<aside
  class="rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-ink-200 bg-white p-6 text-base leading-7 text-ink-600 dark:border-ink-800 dark:bg-ink-900 dark:text-ink-300"
  aria-label="Important limitations"
>
  <p class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">These numbers are estimates</p>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-[72ch]">
    Runtime depends on temperature, battery age, inverter losses, and how your specific device
    behaves. Every hour and watt-hour here is calculated from published specs and engineering
    ranges, not from a lab test of your machine. Treat it as a planning estimate, not a guaranteed
    runtime. A passing wattage check does not verify startup duration, other running loads,
    adapter compatibility, or uninterrupted power. See the <a href="/methodology/" class="underline">methodology</a>
    for the model's limits.
  </p>

  {
    medical && (
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch]">
        <strong class="text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Not medical advice.</strong> A portable power
        station is not a medical device and is not a substitute for the battery system your equipment
        manufacturer specifies. If you depend on a therapy device, confirm your backup plan with
        your equipment provider and your clinician before an outage, not during one.
      </p>
    )
  }

  {
    electrical && (
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch]">
        <strong class="text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Not electrical advice.</strong> Never backfeed
        household wiring through a wall or dryer outlet. This can create a fatal shock hazard.
        Whole-home backup needs a manufacturer-approved, code-compliant transfer or isolation system,
        installed by a qualified electrician where required. Do not connect to household circuits
        without that system.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch] text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">
    A "solar generator" is a battery with an optional solar input. It does not generate power on its
    own, and without panels it is limited to what you charge into it.
  </p>
</aside>
